**Related Spec**: specs/438-return-write-spec-to-native-plan-mode-after-merged-publication/

# File: scripts/__tests__/extension-commands.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/444-exit-native-plan-mode-when-write-spec-finished-is-selected/requirements.md
Feature: Exit native plan mode when write-spec Finished is selected
  Selecting Finished in either write-spec picker left the TUI session in
  native plan mode, so the write-spec cycle could not stop.

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Continue-loop Finished exits plan mode fully
    Given a write-spec continuation running in native plan mode after issue 450 was published
    When the Continue picker returns "Finished — stop writing specs" and the text-only reply ends at the plan-mode decision continuation or terminally
    Then the extension dispatches builtin /plan twice through the focused TUI editor
    And the session mode is recorded as plan_paused and then none
    And the continuation prompt was submitted exactly once and no other command is dispatched

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Initial-picker Finished exits plan mode fully
    Given bare /sdlc-write-spec running in native plan mode
    When the initial picker returns "Finished — stop without writing a spec" and the text-only reply ends at the plan-mode decision continuation or terminally
    Then the extension dispatches builtin /plan twice through the focused TUI editor
    And the last session mode is none and no notification is shown

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Non-Finished selections keep plan mode
    Given a write-spec session in native plan mode
    When a picker returns "#445 — Next issue", "Continue — enter another issue number", custom input "#12", or custom input "abc" and the turn ends terminally
    Then no /plan command is dispatched
    And the session mode stays plan

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Undispatchable exit fails safe
    Given "Finished — stop writing specs" was selected in a write-spec session in native plan mode
    When the reply turn's exit point is reached with no UI, the editor draft "my draft", an unfocused editor, a throwing submit, or a declined exit confirmation
    Then the editor draft is unchanged and no partial command is submitted
    And the warning "NMG SDLC: write-spec finished, but plan mode is still active; /plan exits it." is shown once
    And a later turn end dispatches nothing
    And a non-terminal turn end that is not a plan-mode decision continuation (a tool-call reply, an error or aborted stop, or a session not in plan mode) dispatches nothing

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Post-publication continuation is preserved
    Given merged write-spec publications for issues 400 and 402 in one TUI process
    When each execution turn ends terminally
    Then the Continue prompt is submitted into plan mode exactly once per publication listing every published N-slug
    And a new /sdlc-write-spec invocation resets the published list and a pending Finished exit

  # File: scripts/__tests__/nmg-sdlc-smoke.test.mjs
  @SCN006 @regression
  Scenario: Smoke gate provisions its own fresh issue when no queue is configured
    Given NMG_SDLC_SMOKE_ISSUES is unset and the smoke validation config has a provision need
    When the outer smoke provider runs with Herdr and GitHub available
    Then it drafts exactly one new smoke issue and writes its Approved spec in one owned omp pane
    And it delivers that issue with exact-head merged-PR and closed-issue proof
    And no operator selection or environment variable was needed

  @SCN007 @regression
  Scenario: Provisioning gates are answered with Recommended choices and plan approval
    Given the provisioning session shows a three-question ask and later the plan approval selector
    When the provider polls the session
    Then it sends enter for each question, enter on Submit, and enter on "Approve and execute"
    And it submits "/sdlc-write-spec 179" with a bare issue number
    And it never types text or selects Other

  @SCN008 @regression
  Scenario: Published spec ends provisioning even if the session keeps asking
    Given issue 179 has the spec-created label and a merged "docs: approve spec for #179" pull request
    When the session shows a continuation picker recommending issue 30
    Then the provider closes its owned pane without answering and proceeds to delivery of 179

  @SCN009 @regression
  Scenario: Provisioning failures fail closed without duplicate drafts
    Given provisioning finds zero or two new issues, or an unrecognized blocked gate persists
    When the provider evaluates the session
    Then the result is failed with screen and session evidence, the pane is closed, and the provisioning clone is retained
    And a retry of the same verification identity reuses the recorded issue instead of drafting another

  @SCN010 @regression
  Scenario: Explicit queue keeps priority over provisioning
    Given NMG_SDLC_SMOKE_ISSUES is "#11, 12"
    When the gate runs
    Then no provisioning pane is created and execute runs "#11 #12" exactly as before
